# Vibes-Based Decisions

**`docs/vibes-decisions.md`** tracks every design decision not strongly rooted in evidence — choices made on intuition, convention, or reasonable defaults. Read it before proposing, changing, or questioning any architectural or hyperparameter choice.

Each decision has an **impact level** (High / Med / Low) and a **REVISIT trigger** describing when empirical validation should replace the vibes call.

Key high-impact vibes decisions to be aware of:
- Transformer as backbone (§1.1)
- Top-k action abstraction per turn-node, k ≈ 6 (§9.7)
- Conditional belief sampler design (§10.1)
- Per-slot vs joint-team candidates (§10.2)

When making a design decision: check if `docs/vibes-decisions.md` already covers it, and if so, follow the existing choice unless a REVISIT trigger has fired. When adding a new vibes decision, update the doc rather than scattering rationale across code comments or chat.
